# ============================================================================
#  reference/ IS DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED. DO NOT "CLEAN THIS UP".
# ============================================================================
#  Everything under reference/ originates from third parties and MUST NOT
#  enter this repository's history:
#
#    reference/apk/        the original Magic Portals APK (Asantee Games)
#    reference/extracted/  unpacked APK contents — art, audio, scene/entity
#                          data. We have written permission to REBUILD the
#                          game and REUSE assets; we do NOT have permission
#                          to REDISTRIBUTE them, and a public git repo is
#                          redistribution.
#    reference/ethanon/    Ethanon Engine source (MIT). Vendoring it would be
#                          legal, but it is read-only decoding reference with
#                          its own upstream — it is cloned, not committed.
#                          (It also carries its own nested .git/.)
#
#  Git history is effectively permanent: a commit that lands here is a
#  licensing problem that a later `git rm` does not undo. Whoever is reading
#  this and considering an exception — don't. Put the file somewhere else.
#
#  Consequence, by design: a fresh clone has NO reference/ directory. See
#  README.md for how to recreate it locally.
#
#  DELIBERATELY UNANCHORED (no leading slash): this matches reference/ at ANY
#  depth, not just the repo root. The converter's default input path is
#  cwd-relative, so running it from tools/converter/ would create
#  tools/converter/reference/extracted/ — which a root-anchored "/reference/"
#  would NOT ignore. Do not "tidy" this by adding the slash back.
# ============================================================================
reference/


# --- Godot ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Import cache & editor-generated data. The Godot project root is game/, so in
# practice this is game/.godot/ — left unanchored anyway, for the same reason as
# reference/ above: a second Godot project anywhere in the tree should also be
# covered, and .godot/ is never something worth committing.
.godot/
# Exported builds (APK output — large, reproducible)
/game/android/build/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks

# --- The Supersonic port ------------------------------------------------
# The CMake build tree: tools/parity/port_build.bat configures build/ at the
# root. Unanchored, like reference/ and out/: a build/ at any depth is
# generated. The engine at engine/ is a submodule and keeps its own ignores.
build/

# --- Python converter ----------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/

# --- Converter output staging --------------------------------------------
# The converter reads reference/extracted/ and writes .tscn/assets. Anything
# it emits that still carries Asantee-origin content (textures, audio, level
# data) is subject to the same rule as reference/ above. Keep generated
# output here and it stays out of history until it has been reviewed.
# Unanchored for the same reason as reference/ — the converter's default output
# path is cwd-relative, so out/ can appear below tools/converter/ too.
out/

# --- Converted / original-derived game assets ----------------------------
# DEFAULT-DENY, added 2026-08-04. Same reasoning as reference/ and out/ above,
# applied one step further down the pipeline.
#
# out/ is where the converter STAGES its output; game/assets/ is where reviewed
# output is meant to LAND (CLAUDE.md → Directory layout: "our own + converted
# art"). That promotion step is a human review gate, and until now the gate had
# nothing behind it: game/assets/ was tracked, so a single `git add -A` after a
# conversion run would have committed original art permanently.
#
# WRITTEN AS `**/game/assets/`, NOT `game/assets/` — this is not cosmetic.
# A gitignore pattern containing a slash anywhere but the end is ANCHORED to the
# directory holding the .gitignore, so a bare `game/assets/` matches ONLY the
# repo-root one. `reference/` and `out/` above are single-segment patterns, which
# git treats as matching at any depth — this one is not, and does not get that
# for free. Running the converter from tools/converter/ with `-o game/assets`
# would produce tools/converter/game/assets/, which a bare pattern does NOT
# ignore. Verified with git check-ignore, both at root and nested.
# This is the same defect session 1 fixed on /reference/ — re-introduced here by
# a pattern that merely LOOKS unanchored. Do not "tidy" the `**/` away.
#
# To commit something that is genuinely OURS, force-add it explicitly. The
# friction is the point — it is what makes "did a human look at this?" true:
#
#     git add -f game/assets/ui/our_own_button.png
#
# Do NOT replace this with a negation exception (`!game/assets/...`). Same rule
# as reference/: if a file needs to be committed, force-add that file.
**/game/assets/

# NOTE — data/*.json is deliberately NOT ignored: CLAUDE.md rule 1 requires
# gameplay values to live there as committed data. But the converter GENERATES
# some of it from original level data, so generated .json still needs a human
# read before its first commit. Layout geometry derived from a .esc is Asantee
# level data in a different encoding; hand-authored tuning values are ours.

# --- OS / editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
